      "id": "CVE-2023-4622",
      "published": "2023-09-06T14:15:12.193",
      "lastModified": "2026-09-17T20:16:47.693",
      "vulnStatus": "Modified",
      "description": "A use-after-free vulnerability in the Linux kernel's af_unix component can be exploited to achieve local privilege escalation. The unix_stream_sendpage() function tries to add data to the last skb in the peer's recv queue without locking the queue. Thus there is a race where unix_stream_sendpage() could access an skb locklessly that is being released by garbage collection, resulting in use-after-free. We recommend upgrading past commit 790c2f9d15b594350ae9bca7b236f2b1859de02c (or backported equi",
